+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P1] Shared client service: no streaming, no retry, hardcoded timeout, silent error swallowing (bridge-20261027-client-streaming-retry)
+
+## Problem
+`packages/shared-services/src/services/SupremeAIService.ts` (used by VS Code extension + Electron desktop) fails four reliability/UX disciplines in one file. Verified by direct code read (sha `b6cfa2e5…`):
+
+1. `sendChatMessage()` is a plain `POST /api/chat` — **no streaming**, while the backend has full SSE/WS routes (`api/routes/stream.py`, `swarm_stream.py`, `websocket_hitl.py`) and web studio already streams via `secureSse.ts` + `useServerStream.ts`
+2. `timeout: 10000` hardcoded — Render free-tier cold starts routinely exceed 10 s; `getInlineCompletions` sends the entire prefix as a chat message stub
+3. **Zero retry/backoff** anywhere in the client; `tenacity` exists in only 1 core file
+4. **Silent error swallowing**: `getLearningStats` catch → `{recentActivity: []}`, `getInlineCompletions` catch → `{suggestions: []}`, CodeFlow getters catch → `null` — users see empty UI instead of typed errors; plus `console.log` with eslint-disable in request interceptors
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-085 ❌ timeout/retry/cancel discipline (verified fail)
+- AIQ-093 🟡 streaming only on web
+- AIQ-114 🟡 tower errors are exemplary; studio errors are invisible
+- AIQ-088: 30-second answers either time out or arrive as one frozen block — the single most visible "feels dumber than Monica" difference
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Add `streamChatMessage(request, { onToken, signal })` to the shared service using `fetch` + `ReadableStream` (axios cannot stream in browser contexts), mirroring `secureSse.ts` patterns; keep `sendChatMessage` as a thin wrapper for non-streaming callers
+2. Central `request()` helper: retry ×2 exponential + jitter on network/5xx, 120 s overall with heartbeat, `AbortController` plumbed through
+3. Replace silent catches with a typed `ApiError { code, userMessage, requestId }`; route errors to existing `TelemetryTracker`
+4. Route `getInlineCompletions` to a FIM-capable endpoint with stop sequences + max-token cap + prefix-hash cache
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] Desktop + VS Code render tokens progressively; cancel stops server-side generation
+- [ ] Killing the primary API mid-chat shows a typed reconnecting state, not an empty screen
+- [ ] No bare `console.log` in production paths (leveled logger only)
+- [ ] p95 completion latency < 800 ms for inline completions
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** streaming is the highest-leverage perceived-intelligence fix; the backend already supports it — only the client lags.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) rewriting the service class — out of cohesive-task sizing; (b) polling-based progress — strictly worse UX and more load.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P1-high` `area:studio` `area:vscode` `AIQ:085` `AIQ:093` `AIQ:114` `AIQ:088`
